<title>USA: NYPA pushes 780 MW nuke unit restart to weekend.</title>
<headline>NYPA pushes 780 MW nuke unit restart to weekend.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York Power Authority (NYPA) delayed the restart of its 780 megawatt (MW) Fitzpatrick nuclear power station in Scriba, N.Y., to &quot;sometime over the weekend,&quot; a utility spokesman said Friday.</p>
<p>NYPA earlier hoped the plant would resume power production Thursday.</p>
<p>The Fitzpatrick plant tripped off line Monday when a technician caused an electrical short, which in turn opened the generator output breakers and automatically shut down the reactor.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
</text>
